Tab Query
Tab Query
Define a query that finds objects according to the criteria you type into the cells of the list on the tab
Query.
Remarks
Before you can type in data, click the Inheritance check box so that it looks like this 
 .
Select the number of opening Parentheses, type in an Attribute, select a Condition, a Value, select the
number of closing Parentheses, select an Operator, and type in a Comment. Select the Frame that the
AttributeExplorer queries.
Select the check box Include Subframes to also query any Frames which located within the selected
Frame.
Select Include MUs to also include the parts (MUs) in your model in your query.
Tab Query
Plant Simulation Help 11-4423
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Spelled out in code our query reads like this:
Name Expr Station.* and ((XPos > 100 and YPos = 200) or ExitStrategy = 
Cyclic)
To manipulate the contents of the list, use the commands on the Context Menu of Embedded Lists.
