Condition [AttributeExplorer]
Click in the cell once with the left mouse button and select a Condition from the drop-down list.
Remarks
You can select one of these settings:
• < (less than)
• <= (less than or equal to)
• > (greater than)
• >= (greater than or equal to)
• = (equal to), compares attributes of data type real, length, weight, speed, and time for the exact value
• ~= (equal to, case-insensitive) compares if strings are equal not considering lower and upper-casing, or
compares if the values of attributes are about equal
• /= (not equal to)
• Expr, which is a regular expression, compare regex_search. You might, for example, type in ^Inf,
which finds any word beginning with Inf.
• Exists, checks if the object has the designated attribute or not.
Then, type the value into the corresponding cell in the column Value.
Condition [AttributeExplorer]
Plant Simulation Help 11-4427
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

